ONVIF profile from the live stream for go2rtc v1.9.15 (7c05066).
The ONVIF server advertises the stream's real size and frame rate, read from the SPS of its
running config producer (a producer a client pushed does not count), or the ONVIF_* env values,
instead of a fixed 1080p30 at 8192 kbit/s. DecodeSPS is hardened against crafted SPS: the frame
rate is computed in uint64 (no division by zero), a pic order cycle over 255 is rejected, and
SPS.Size ignores a size outside 1..8192. SystemReboot, which upstream answered with an exit of
the whole process one second later (unauthenticated, so any LAN host could keep the copy down),
gets an ActionNotSupported SOAP fault and changes nothing; SetSystemDateAndTime already only
answers OK, and no other action changes state. Comes with its own tests
(go test ./pkg/h264/ ./internal/streams/ ./internal/onvif/).

